;; ADT-CYCLE-TLIST. The cell that pins the LLMLL.md §5.3.3 sentence.
;;
;; `Tree` is recursive THROUGH A LIST. `admissibleDatatype`'s `sumOf` descends
;; `TSumType` and `TCustom` only, so it never sees the cycle and calls `Tree`
;; admissible. §5.3.3 says that is correct and does not need repair: the `list`
;; carrier lowers to the uninterpreted `Lst` sort, so the emitted declaration is
;; acyclic and no defining equation exists for the solver to unfold.
;;
;; The spec sentence grants a capability, and this cell is what guards it: such a
;; type may be CARRIED opaquely through a verified function. The body projects
;; the `int` component only, so the VC is QF-LIA over `pair2_0 s`.
;;
;; Before v0.23.11 this fell back, and NOT because of the firewall. The pair
;; parameter had no binder at all, so `FQ-FREEVAR-GUARD-1` routed it. That was
;; the free-symbol accident; `PAIR-PROJ-LET-1` removed it.
(export take-first)
(type Tree (| Leaf) (| Node list[Tree]))
(def-shell take-first [s: (int, Tree)] -> int
  (post (>= result 0))
  (let [(n (first s))]
    (if (>= n 0) n 0)))
